+# Diagnostics schema (FeedGate 2.1.1)
+
+Schema version: `4`. Previous exports (schema 3, produced by 2.1.0) remain
+readable JSON with the same core fields; see Compatibility below.
+
+The export is privacy-safe by design. It is a record of decisions and
+counters, not a record of content.
+
+## Export envelope
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `format` | always `feedgate-diagnostics` |
+| `version` | schema version, `4` |
+| `extensionVersion` | released extension version, `2.1.1` |
+| `rubric` | semantic rubric, `feed-v2.1.0` |
+| `build` | fingerprint object, see below |
+| `generatedAt` | ISO timestamp of the export |
+| `environment` | literal `chrome-extension` |
+| `privacy` | short human-readable privacy statement |
+| `connection` | transport, model, key readiness, verification time, vault and cooldown state |
+| `settings` | effective policy settings (sites, preset, mode, categories, limits, counts) |
+| `metrics` | session counters, see below |
+| `daily` | provider requests used today (`date`, `requests`) |
+| `queue`, `active`, `cached` | queue depth, in-flight count, cache entries |
+| `permissions` | which optional hosts are currently granted |
+| `pages` | recent per-tab page summaries (retention: last 100, exports keep 24 h) |
+| `decisions` | retained decision window, newest first, up to 150 entries |
+
+### Build fingerprint
+
+```json
+"build": {
+  "release": "2.1.1",
+  "rubric": "feed-v2.1.0",
+  "policy": "policy-2.1.1",
+  "detector": "ad-2.1.1",
+  "extraction": "extract-2.1.1",
+  "schema": 4
+}
+```
+
+The fingerprint lets a support reader tell which layer changed. The rubric is
+intentionally unchanged from 2.1.0; the policy, detector and extraction are
+not.
+
+## Decision entries
+
+Each entry in `decisions`:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `at` | epoch ms |
+| `site` | `x`, `reddit`, `linkedin`, `facebook`, `instagram` or `demo` |
+| `action` | `allow`, `dim`, `collapse` |
+| `wouldAction` | present in Observe Only when the action would have differed |
+| `source` | `policy`, `jev`, `local`, `allowlist`, `override`, `protection`, `unclassified` |
+| `rule` | machine-readable rule name, e.g. `feed_spam`, `below_noise_thresholds` |
+| `category` | filtering category when a category branch applied |
+| `protected` | true only when protection was applied |
+| `protectionEligible` | true when the estimates alone met the useful/original thresholds |
+| `conflict` | true for the documented spam-and-value conflict dim |
+| `sufficient` | evidence estimate that gated the decision, or null |
+| `scores` | named estimates: `unwantedAd`, `feedSpam`, `bait`, `lowSignal`, `useful`, `original`, `risk`, `sufficient` |
+| `adEvidence` | verified/adapter evidence summary or null, see below |
+| `model` | provider model that produced the estimates |
+| `latencyMs` | recorded classification latency |
+| `cached` | true when estimates came from the local cache |
+| `error` | error code string or null |
+
+### Ad evidence summary
+
+When a local action was considered, `adEvidence` contains:
+
+```json
+{
+  "status": "verified",
+  "markerKind": "x_data_promoted_attribute",
+  "selectorId": "x-attr-data-promoted",
+  "ownerMatched": true,
+  "renderedLabel": null,
+  "evidenceKind": "platform_metadata",
+  "scope": "outer_post"
+}
+```
+
+`status` is `verified`, `ambiguous` or `none`. `markerKind` is an enum from
+the reviewed detector rules, never free DOM text. `scope` is `outer_post`,
+`quote`, `unrelated` or `unknown`.
+
+## Metrics
+
+Counters: `decisions`, `protected` (protection applied), `usefulPromotions`
+(kept with a promotional signal), `requests` (provider attempts), `classified`
+(successful responses), `cacheHits`, `filterDecisions` (hidden or dimmed,
+including observe-only candidates), `errors`, `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`,
+`lastLatencyMs`, `lastModel`, `lastError`.
+
+Counters persist in the browser session and survive a worker restart; the
+history window does not grow beyond its retention size.
+
+## Retention
+
+| Store | Limit |
+| --- | --- |
+| Decision log | newest 150 entries |
+| Page reports | newest 100 tabs, exported only if within 24 h |
+| Decision cache | 1600 entries |
+| Saved post choices | 2000 keys |
+| In-flight queue | 150 jobs |
+
+A 2.1.0 export with 150 retained entries and larger session counters is
+consistent with this design: counters are cumulative, the array is a window.
+
+## Privacy boundaries
+
+Exports never contain: post text, quoted text, author names or handles, page
+URLs or permalinks, credentials, the API key, vault contents, custom
+instruction text, cosmetic selector text, cache or feedback hashes. `scores`
+are model estimates, not facts or identity labels. Incident exports supplied
+by the owner are used in `tests/incident.test.mjs` only as a fixture to verify
+counter arithmetic; the fixture is not part of the shipped runtime.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+* Settings schema remains `3`; settings exports keep the `feedgate-settings`
+  envelope with `version: 3`. Imports accept version 3 and version 2 (2.0
+  exports are migrated to safe 2.1 defaults; old thresholds are not mapped).
+* Runtime state schema is `4`. A session state written by an older schema is
+  dropped instead of replayed, so stale cached decisions cannot contaminate a
+  new release.
+* Diagnostics exports from 2.1.0 (`version: 3`) can still be read by humans
+  and by the incident test; new exports use `version: 4` and add the `build`
+  block, `protectionEligible` and `adEvidence` fields.
