+# Requirement matrix: FeedGate 2.1.1 evidence-based filtering repair
+
+This matrix maps every requirement of the repair task to its implementation and
+to the test or evidence that demonstrates it. Statuses are `MET`, `NOT_MET` or
+`INSUFFICIENT`. Every status reflects work actually executed in this workspace;
+nothing here is copied from a previous completion report.
+
+This document is a self-check prepared by the implementing agent. It is not an
+independent acceptance or an external audit.
+
+Evidence files referenced below:
+
+- `evidence/unit-tests.tap` - full Node test run (118 tests, all passing)
+- `evidence/browser-dom-tests.json` - Chromium DOM/UI scenarios (46, all passing)
+- `evidence/extension-smoke.json` - unpacked-extension smoke test (7 checks, all passing)
+- `evidence/release-checks.json` - release integrity checks (8, all passing)
+- `evidence/baseline/` - immutable 2.1.0 baseline (inventory, hashes, test logs, incident analysis)
+- `evidence/after/` - copies of the 2.1.1 verification artefacts
+- `tests/fixtures/incident/` - the two supplied privacy-safe diagnostic exports
+
+## 1. Release gates from the task
+
+| Gate | Status | Where it is demonstrated |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsupported generic markers cannot produce a verified platform ad | MET | `src/core.js` `sanitizeAdEvidence` downgrade rules; `src/adapters.js` `detectAdEvidence`; tests `tests/core.test.mjs` ("ad evidence stays verified only with ownership..."), browser scenarios AD01/AD04/AD05/AD06/AD08/AD09 |
+| Reviewed true positive still works; unverified adapters fall back conservatively | MET | `src/adapters.js` per-adapter rules; browser scenarios AD07 (`local_ad`), AD10, AD14; `tests/worker.test.mjs` 25 (local collapse, zero provider calls) |
+| No newly aggressive semantic rule from the anonymous log scores | MET | Thresholds unchanged in `src/core.js` (`risk .94`, `feedSpam .90`, `unwantedAd .85`, `bait .88`; Low-signal filler still `off`); `docs/DECISION_POLICY.md` documents this explicitly |
+| R1/R2 explanations truthful and no bypass of qualified rules | MET | `decide()` tail returns `promotion_signal_alone` only when no other noise estimate reaches 0.60, otherwise `below_noise_thresholds`; replay tests R1-R6 in `tests/policy-v21.test.mjs` |
+| Parsing preserves named probabilities and rejects malformed data | MET | `parseResponse` strict contract; API01-API03 tests in `tests/core.test.mjs`; malformed-response tests in `tests/worker.test.mjs` and `tests/http.test.mjs` |
+| Source, shipped runtime, versions and hashes agree | MET | `npm run build` + `npm run release:check` (byte comparison `static/` and `src/` vs `extension/`); release checks 5 in `evidence/release-checks.json`; smoke test reports release 2.1.1 |
+| Privacy, key handling, migration, overrides, Observe Only and stale-result handling survive | MET | `tests/diagnostics-v21.test.mjs` (privacy, secret scanning), `tests/worker.test.mjs` (vault, consent, lock, export/import), browser scenarios `observe`/`keep_this_post`/`keyboard_reveal`/stale/recycled |
+| Runtime has no local bridge dependency | MET | Release checks 6-7 (no localhost/127.0.0.1, no executable installers); smoke test tracks and rejects localhost traffic |
+| Test counts and live-validation claims match actual execution | MET | Counts from executed runs only; live provider and signed-in-site validation labelled `INSUFFICIENT` below |
+
+## 2. Evidence discipline
+
