+# Root cause notes: FeedGate 2.1.1
+
+This document separates what was confirmed from what remains an open question.
+It answers the repair task directly: it was written from the source tree, the
+reproduced test fixtures and the supplied diagnostics, not from previous
+assistant reports.
+
+## Confirmed defects (reproduced in tests before the fix)
+
+### 1. The local ad detector was a broad heuristic, not evidence
+
+`src/adapters.js` (2.1.0) used one function, `isSponsored`, that returned a
+plain boolean. A single descendant element with
+`data-testid="placementTracking"` was enough, regardless of ownership or
+visibility. A 250-node scan of `span` and `[aria-label]` text accepted any of
+several localized words, plus a bare `Ad` span. Nothing proved that a label
+belonged to the outer post, that it was rendered, or that the placement was
+paid.
+
+Consequence: organic posts that happened to contain tracking wrappers or the
+word "Sponsored" somewhere inside them could be collapsed with the reason
+`Platform-labelled ad`, before any model judgment existed. The supplied
+diagnostics show 28 such local collapses in one retained X window and no
+semantic filtering at all in that window.
+
+After the fix an action requires a structured evidence record with
+`status: "verified"`, outer-post ownership, a known marker kind encoded as an
+enum and a rendered or platform-metadata basis. `placementTracking` alone is
+only `ambiguous`, and ambiguous evidence follows the normal semantic path.
+`tests/browser.py` scenarios AD01-AD14 cover this; `tests/worker.test.mjs`
+proves that a legacy boolean flag no longer hides anything.
+
+### 2. A legacy boolean survived sanitization as usable ad proof
+
+`sanitizeRecord` accepted `sponsored: true` from any caller and
+`inferenceState` forwarded it to the provider as
+`platform_sponsored_marker_observed: true`. Old cached flags and hand-built
+messages could therefore keep producing local collapses after the marker had
+disappeared.
+
+After the fix a boolean `sponsored` value is migrated to `ambiguous` and is
+never usable as local proof; the provider only sees a verified flag. Covered
+by `ad evidence stays verified only with ownership, scope and a known marker`
+in `tests/core.test.mjs` and by worker tests 25-26.
+
+### 3. `promotion_signal_alone` was reported too broadly
+
+The final fall-through of `decide()` reported the reason
+`Promotional intent alone is not a hiding rule` whenever `unwantedAd >= 0.6`,
+even when `feedSpam`, `bait` or `risk` were also elevated (just below their
+thresholds) and nothing was actually decided. Replays R1 and R2 from the
+supplied diagnostics were kept with that rule name, which overstates what the
+policy checked.
+
+After the fix `promotion_signal_alone` is only reported when
+`unwantedAd >= 0.6` and no other noise estimate reaches `0.6`. Otherwise the
+decision reports the truthful `below_noise_thresholds`
+("No category threshold was met; kept"). Replayed in
+`tests/policy-v21.test.mjs` (Appendix B rows R1-R6) and asserted in
+`tests/incident.test.mjs` as historical behaviour, not as accuracy labels.
+
+### 4. Reddit titles could be duplicated in the extracted text
+
+`extract()` for Reddit unconditionally prepended the `post-title` attribute to
+the text already collected from `[slot="title"]`, producing a repeated title in
+the payload. After the fix the title is only prepended when it is not already
+present. Covered by `EXT01` in `tests/browser.py`.
+
+### 5. The extraction reader and the shipped runtime drifted
+
+The 2.0 archive's `isSponsored` was reviewed historically; the 2.1.0 tree
+still contained the same logic. `npm run release:check` now also compares every
+static asset and source file byte-for-byte with `extension/`, and the build
+fingerprint in diagnostics makes a stale worker visible. Covered by release
+check 5 and `tests/extension_smoke.py`.
+
+## Historical leads that were confirmed as code, not as live incidents
+
+* The 2.0 archive (`FeedGate-2.0.0.zip`,
+  sha256 `ee4a9c0fd698d030ed6c83948a8e112fedaf3fd568523d4e3e04412f7f7463d3`)
+  contained the same detector; it is the origin of the code that was fixed,
+  but no claim is made that every locally collapsed item in the diagnostics
+  was organic.
+* The 2.0 protection guard used `value >= .70 || contribution >= .75`. The
+  renamed 2.1 thresholds were `.70 / .75` as well. Observed `protected: 0` in
+  the diagnostics is consistent with the recorded `useful` and `original`
+  values (for example `0.67` and `0.72`), so the counter was not broken. The
+  thresholds were lowered to `.65 / .70` as a documented engineering choice
+  that keeps more marginally useful content visible; the sufficiency guard was
+  not changed.
+
+## Open hypotheses (not reproduced, no live validation available)
+
+* Whether the specific post in the supplied screenshot was organic: the DOM is
+  not available, only the reason string and the description. Local collapses
+  in the window did come from the loose detector, but the accuracy of every
+  individual collapse cannot be re-labeled from the export.
+* Whether the provider's estimates cluster because of rubric wording,
+  input construction or model calibration. The parser, mapping and thresholds
+  were verified; calibration remains an open evaluation question, not a
+  verified defect.
+* Whether any owned `promotedIndicator` observed in the wild is
+  personalized rather than paid. The detector treats a rendered indicator
+  owned by the outer post as verified platform metadata; it does not claim
+  to know the campaign behind it.
+
+## What this repair deliberately does not do
+
+* It does not lower category thresholds to make more posts disappear.
+* It does not enable LowSignal on upgrade.
+* It does not convert the anonymous Reddit score vectors into keyword rules.
+* It does not label authors, accounts or professions.
+* It does not weaken privacy, key handling, consent or the no-bridge design.
