+DOM scenarios cover the previous 31 cases plus tracking-wrapper false positives, video and quoted-media posts, sibling cards, labels in names, links and alt text, hidden templates, strict attribute semantics, off-viewport rendered markers, marker removal, the local-ad toggle, self-loop stability, Reddit ownership rules, duplicate-title prevention, extraction limitations, UI-text exclusion, extraction stability and the stale-content-script reload prompt.
+
+The extension smoke test loads the real `extension/` folder into a local Chromium profile, waits for the service worker, reads the release version, opens the demo feed and verifies that a card names the platform label, plus no localhost traffic, no page errors and no worker errors.
+
+## Fixture provenance
+
+All adapter and policy fixtures are synthetic HTML and assigned scores. Provider responses are controlled implementations, not captured traffic. `tests/fixtures/incident/` contains two real 2.1.0 diagnostic exports supplied by the owner; by schema design they contain no post text, authors, keys or full URLs, and they are used only for count replay, never as accuracy labels. Screenshots with `fixture` in the name show synthetic harness state, not live provider results.
 
